```

The `getMin` function simply retrieves the top element from the `minStack`, which holds the minimum elements corresponding to the elements in the main stack. If the `minStack` is empty, it throws an `EmptyStackException`. This implementation ensures that the minimum element can be retrieved in constant time, O(1), without affecting the time complexity of the push and pop operations.

