### Problem:
You are tasked with creating a program that analyzes the frequency of words in a given text file. Your program should read a text file and output the frequency of each word in the file. Words are considered to be sequences of characters separated by spaces. The program should ignore punctuation and consider words in a case-insensitive manner. Additionally, the program should exclude common stop words such as "the", "and", "of", "in", etc. The output should display each word along with its frequency in descending order of frequency.

For example, given the following text file "sample.txt":
```
This is a sample text file. This file contains some sample text for testing the word frequency program.
```
The program should output:
```
sample: 2
text: 2
file: 2
this: 2
contains: 1
for: 1
frequency: 1
is: 1
program: 1
some: 1
testing: 1
```

### Solution:
```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class WordFrequencyAnalyzer {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String fileName = "sample.txt";
        Map<String, Integer> wordFrequency = new HashMap<>();

        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(fileName))) {
            String line;
            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
                line = line.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z ]", "").toLowerCase();
                String[] words = line.split("\\s+");
                for (String word : words) {
                    if (!word.isEmpty() && !isStopWord(word)) {
                        wordFrequency.put(word, wordFrequency.getOrDefault(word, 0) + 1);
                    }
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }

        wordFrequency.entrySet().stream()
                .sorted(Map.Entry.<String, Integer>comparingByValue().reversed())
                .forEach(entry -> System.out.println(entry.getKey() + ": " + entry.getValue()));
    }

    private static boolean isStopWord(String word) {
        String[] stopWords = {"the", "and", "of", "in", "for", "on", "with", "at", "to", "from"};
        for (String stopWord : stopWords) {
            if (word.equals(stopWord)) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

This solution reads the text file line by line, removes punctuation, converts words to lowercase, and splits them by spaces. It then populates a map with word frequencies, excluding stop words. Finally, it sorts the map entries by frequency in descending order and prints the word frequencies.

