You are tasked with implementing a program that processes a large collection of text data to find the most frequent n-grams (sequences of n words) within the text. To achieve this, you will need to develop a MapReduce program using Hadoop. The input data will consist of a set of text documents, and the output should be the top k most frequent n-grams along with their respective counts.

Your task is to implement the Reducer class for the MapReduce program. The Reducer should aggregate the intermediate results from the Mapper and output the top k most frequent n-grams. To accomplish this, you will utilize a PriorityQueue to efficiently maintain the top k n-grams based on their counts.

The Reducer class should have the following signature:
```java
public static class NgramReducer extends Reducer<Text, LongWritable, NullWritable, Text> {
    private int k; // The number of top n-grams to output
    private PriorityQueue<NgramCount> queue; // Priority queue to store the top k n-grams

    // Initialize the reducer with the value of k and instantiate the priority queue
    protected void setup(Context context) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Retrieve the value of k from the configuration
        k = context.getConfiguration().getInt("top_k", 10);
        // Initialize the priority queue with a custom comparator to order n-grams by count
        queue = new PriorityQueue<>(k, Comparator.comparingLong(NgramCount::getCount).reversed());
    }

    // Process the intermediate results and maintain the top k n-grams in the priority queue
    public void reduce(Text key, Iterable<LongWritable> values, Context context) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        long count = 0;
        for (LongWritable value : values) {
            count += value.get();
        }
        // Add the n-gram and its count to the priority queue
        queue.offer(new NgramCount(key.toString(), count));
        // If the queue size exceeds k, remove the least frequent n-gram
        if (queue.size() > k) {
            queue.poll();
        }
    }

    // Output the top k n-grams along with their counts
    protected void cleanup(Context context) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Output the top k n-grams in descending order of frequency
        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            NgramCount ngramCount = queue.poll();
            context.write(NullWritable.get(), new Text(ngramCount.getNgram() + "\t" + ngramCount.getCount()));
        }
    }
}
```

