Write a Java program that fulfills the requirements outlined above. Your program should be able to handle different combinations of command-line arguments and execute the JAR file with the specified Java options.

### Solution:
```java
import java.io.IOException;

public class JarExecutor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        if (args.length < 1) {
            System.out.println("Usage: java JarExecutor [-o <java_options>] <jar_file>");
            return;
        }

        String javaOptions = "";
        String jarFile = "";

        // Parse command-line arguments
        for (int i = 0; i < args.length; i++) {
            if (args[i].equals("-o")) {
                if (i + 1 < args.length) {
                    javaOptions = args[i + 1];
                    i++; // Skip the next argument
                } else {
                    System.out.println("Error: Missing java_options after -o");
                    return;
                }
            } else {
                jarFile = args[i];
            }
        }

        // Execute the JAR file with the specified Java options
        try {
            ProcessBuilder processBuilder = new ProcessBuilder("java", javaOptions, "-jar", jarFile);
            Process process = processBuilder.start();
            int exitCode = process.waitFor();
            if (exitCode == 0) {
                System.out.println("JAR file executed successfully");
            } else {
                System.out.println("Error: Failed to execute JAR file");
            }
        } catch (IOException | InterruptedException e) {
            System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

This Java program, `JarExecutor`, accepts command-line arguments and executes a Java JAR file with the specified Java options. It parses the command-line arguments to extract the Java options and the JAR file path, then uses `ProcessBuilder` to execute the JAR file with the provided Java options. The program handles potential errors during the execution and provides appropriate feedback to the user.

