### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a custom annotation processor in Java. The goal is to create an annotation called `CustomAnnotation` that can be used to mark methods within a class. When this annotation is present on a method, the processor should generate a new method in the same class that logs a message before and after the original method's execution.

Your task is to create the `CustomAnnotation` annotation and the corresponding annotation processor that will generate the logging method.

The `CustomAnnotation` should have the following properties:
- It should be applicable to methods only.
- It should have a single attribute called `value` of type `String` which represents the log message to be printed.

The annotation processor should:
- Identify all methods in a class that are annotated with `CustomAnnotation`.
- Generate a new method in the same class for each annotated method, which logs the message specified in the `value` attribute before and after invoking the original method.

Your solution should include the definition of the `CustomAnnotation` annotation, the annotation processor, and an example usage of the annotation.

### Solution:
```java
// CustomAnnotation.java
import java.lang.annotation.ElementType;
import java.lang.annotation.Retention;
import java.lang.annotation.RetentionPolicy;
import java.lang.annotation.Target;

@Retention(RetentionPolicy.SOURCE)
@Target(ElementType.METHOD)
public @interface CustomAnnotation {
    String value();
}

// CustomAnnotationProcessor.java
import javax.annotation.processing.AbstractProcessor;
import javax.annotation.processing.RoundEnvironment;
import javax.annotation.processing.SupportedAnnotationTypes;
import javax.annotation.processing.SupportedSourceVersion;
import javax.lang.model.SourceVersion;
import javax.lang.model.element.Element;
import javax.lang.model.element.Modifier;
import javax.lang.model.element.TypeElement;
import javax.lang.model.element.VariableElement;
import javax.tools.JavaFileObject;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.PrintWriter;
import java.util.Set;

@SupportedAnnotationTypes("CustomAnnotation")
@SupportedSourceVersion(SourceVersion.RELEASE_8)
public class CustomAnnotationProcessor extends AbstractProcessor {
    @Override
    public boolean process(Set<? extends TypeElement> annotations, RoundEnvironment roundEnv) {
        for (Element element : roundEnv.getElementsAnnotatedWith(CustomAnnotation.class)) {
            if (element instanceof VariableElement) {
                VariableElement methodElement = (VariableElement) element;
                String methodName = methodElement.getSimpleName().toString();
                String logMessage = methodElement.getAnnotation(CustomAnnotation.class).value();

                String className = ((TypeElement) methodElement.getEnclosingElement()).getQualifiedName().toString();

                generateLoggingMethod(className, methodName, logMessage);
            }
        }
        return true;
    }

    private void generateLoggingMethod(String className, String methodName, String logMessage) {
        String loggingMethodName = "log_" + methodName;
        String loggingMethodBody = String.format(
                "System.out.println(\"Logging: %s\");\n" +
                        "%s();\n" +
                        "System.out.println(\"Finished logging\");",
                logMessage, methodName);

        String generatedMethod = String.format(
                "private void %s() {\n" +
                        "    %s\n" +
                        "}\n", loggingMethodName, loggingMethodBody);

        try {
            JavaFileObject fileObject = processingEnv.getFiler().createSourceFile(className);
            try (PrintWriter writer = new PrintWriter(fileObject.openWriter())) {
                writer.print(generatedMethod);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}

// Example usage in a class
public class MyClass {
    @CustomAnnotation("Entering method doSomething")
    public void doSomething() {
        // Method implementation
    }
}
```

